# «Include removed dealers»

Origin: `plans/plan-totales-income-centavos/PLAN.md` (D3, T1.7 and §4). Applies to every screen or export of PRO
with totals by dealer (today: Income by Dealer, Production vs Goal, Business KPIs › Billing and Open AR, Invoices).

## What a removed dealer is

A dealer the company removed with **«Remove»** in legacy (Dealers › dealer menu, Admin General only) **after**
migration 017: it has a row in `DEALER_REL_REMOVED` of that company and **no** row in `DEALER_REL` with it. Dealers
removed before the record existed never enter (D8). A dealer removed and added again with «Add» is back in the combo
and is not counted twice.

## Do

- **Front:** use `useRemovedDealersSwitch` (`hooks/use-removed-dealers-available.ts`) and `RemovedDealersSwitch`
  (`components/filters/removed-dealers-switch.tsx`), next to «Filter by completion date».
- **Show it only when the endpoint says there is something:** `GET /srs/kpis/billing/removed-dealers-available` with
  the screen's range (none = whole history) and its own «Filter by completion date». Plus `user.isSystemAdmin` and
  «All dealers» in the combo. Off by default; when it stops showing (range, combo or filter changed) it goes back to
  off.
- Off = exactly the dealers of the combo (same totals as before the switch existed).
- The value goes as `includeRemovedDealers` to every request of the screen that has totals by dealer (and in its
  `queryKey`), including the cards without period of the same screen («Owed, all dates» of Invoices).
- With the switch on, the export says it in **Report Info** (one line «Include removed dealers: Yes — <names>», with
  the removed dealers that have rows in that file; just «Yes» when none).
- **Mark the rows** (§5): every row of a removed dealer shows `RemovedDealerBadge`
  (`components/filters/removed-dealer-badge.tsx`, «Removed» / «Eliminado» with its tooltip) and exports
  «<dealer> (removed)» / «(eliminado)». Which dealers: `removedIds` of `useRemovedDealersSwitch` (every removed dealer
  of the company, with or without money). Names in Report Info / Summary: only the ones with rows in the file.
- Texts: EN «Include removed dealers» / help «Adds dealers that were removed from your dealer list but still have
  invoices or Work Orders with your company in these dates.»; ES «Incluir dealers eliminados» / «Suma los dealers que
  se eliminaron de tu lista de dealers pero todavía tienen invoices o Work Orders con tu empresa en estas fechas.»
  (D7 and D9, approved word by word).
- **Backend:** the dealer filter goes through `buildDealerRestrictionClause` / `buildDealerFilterSql`
  (`src/srs/shared/kpi/srs-kpi-dealer-filter.ts`) with `removedDealersProvider(filter)`, and the query filters its
  **data table** by `id_dealer_provider` = the session provider (not only `c`).

## Never

- Show the switch without asking the endpoint, or with dealers picked one by one in the combo.
- Take the provider from the request: it is always the session one (JWT); the proxy drops `idDealerProvider`.
- Honour the flag for users with assigned dealers or external users: `includeRemovedDealersForSession` forces it to
  false, and the endpoint answers `available: false` without querying.
- Count «dealers with no `DEALER_REL` row» without `DEALER_REL_REMOVED`: that brings the dealers removed before the
  record (D8).
